# Security response headers for the Cloudflare-served site (floodwarning.net).
# Cloudflare Workers static assets apply these to served files; the /api/* Worker
# routes set their own headers (see worker/index.js). GitHub Pages ignores this
# file, so the github.io copy is unaffected.
#
# Deliberately conservative: only headers that cannot change how the app loads
# its own resources. `frame-ancestors 'none'` blocks clickjacking without a
# resource-blocking CSP (a full script-src policy is a tested follow-up, since
# the app relies on inline handlers and several CDNs). See the security
# appraisal, finding M-3.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
